data/raw/*.csv
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
webapp/frontend/dist/
.env
*.log
*.zip
# data/synthetic/, defend/artifacts/, and generate/fidelity_report.json are
# DELIBERATELY tracked (not ignored) -- they're the actual output of the Generate and
# Defend pillars (synthetic attacks, trained model, evaluation reports). Previously
# gitignored, which meant the GitHub repo contained only the code that COULD regenerate
# these, not the specific run they were documented from -- since LLM-driven generation
# is non-deterministic, "fresh clone + rerun" could silently produce different numbers
# than what's written in the docx/README. Committing the actual artifacts fixes that.
